          "kicker": "Red Roses loss",
          "heading": "England women's 41-match unbeaten run ends, Mitchell's side beaten 24-21 by Canada",
          "body": "The Red Roses' 41-match unbeaten run ended in Toronto, where Canada came back to win 24-21 thanks to Shoshanah Seumanutafa's try three minutes from time. It was England's first defeat since November 2022, when New Zealand beat them in the World Cup final, and Canada's first win over them since 2016. Coach John Mitchell said: \"We're disappointed by the result but there was some very good things in our performance. So we'll stick to our processes.\""
