          "kicker": "Travel scare",
          "heading": "France winger Louis Bielle-Biarrey temporarily denied UK entry at Bristol Airport",
          "body": "Four Bordeaux Bègles players, including France winger Louis Bielle-Biarrey, were stranded at Bristol Airport ahead of their Investec Champions Cup opener against Gloucester. Loosehead prop Matis Perchaud, loose forward Romain Gardrat and Tonga tighthead prop Toma Taufa were held with him, along with a fitness coach, over an administrative problem: their electronic travel permits were linked to passports renewed earlier this year, with no new authorisations obtained. The club contacted the French embassy in London, the issue was eventually resolved, and the players rejoined their teammates."
