          "body": "Leinster's 48-23 win over Clermont in Pool 1 of the Investec Champions Cup came with a cost for Ireland: number eight Jack Conan left with a wrist injury. Planet Rugby called it the only sour note, with Ireland's Nations Championship campaign resuming three weeks on. Sam Prendergast, scoring 14 points, is back in the conversation at fly-half, with Jack Crowley currently sidelined."
