          "body": "Scotland women's pathway just got a fresh voice: Caity Mattinson, who won 37 caps as a scrum-half before retiring in September 2025, has been appointed Scottish Rugby's new Pathways Skills Coach. Her remit covers talent identification, player profiling and specialist kicking and half-back coaching across the women's National Talent Pathway and National Academy. She also worked with Scotland Women's U21s during the 2026 Six Nations. \"I can’t wait to get started.\""
